'''Raven's Peak Sky Rail''' was a series of fast-moving sky rails suspended from rail lines<ref name="DB">{{Databank|raven-s-peak-sky-rail|Raven's Peak Sky Rail}}</ref> on the [[planet]] [[Eriadu]].<ref name="The Summit" /> It was used during the [[Imperial Era]] to access [[Raven's Peak]], the compound of [[Governor]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]].<ref name="Plan 99" /> The sky rails of the Raven's Peak Rail Line consisted of two crate-shaped cars on parallel tracks, which shuffled troops back and forth.<ref name="DB" /> During or after [[18 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{TBBDate|215}}</ref> [[Clone Force 99]] [[Bombing of Raven's Peak|infiltrated Raven's Peak]] through the sky rail, after disabling its sensor.<ref name="The Summit" />

==Description==
Raven's Peak sky rail consisted of a network of fast-moving twin-[[train|car]] [[Raven's Peak sky train|sky trains]]<ref name="DB" /> that moved along two reinforced rail lines suspended from the [[mountain]]s around [[Raven's Peak]] fortress on the [[planet]] [[Eriadu]]. The trains were connected to the track via a complex assembly of powered interlocking gears that rotated,<ref name="The Summit" /> thus moving the trains along the sky line.<ref name="DB" /> A number of maintenance stations were located on the sky line's support pylons to allow for easy access to the line's [[computer]].<ref name="The Summit" />

The rail line began on the small [[Raven's Peak starfighter depot|starfighter depot]] on the lower hills of the mountain, where two observation posts were also located overlooking the valley below. From there, the line was mostly suspended on the air until it reached a station in the [[hangar]] level of the fortress itself, although in some spots it came close to nearby mountaintops. These parts of the line were equipped with military-grade [[perimeter sensor]]s that were able to detect [[Species|organic]] movement nearby in order to deter potential hijackers.<ref name="The Summit" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Raven's Peak Sky Rail first appeared in the fifteenth episode of the [[The Bad Batch Season 2|second season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars: The Bad Batch]]'', "[[The Summit]]." It later appeared in the sixteenth and final episode of the season, "[[Plan 99 (episode)|Plan 99]]." Both episodes premiered on [[Disney+]] on [[March 29]], [[2023]].<ref name="The Summit" /><ref name="Plan 99">{{TBB|Plan 99 (episode)}}</ref>

